        "char_feng_jin_huang",
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_feng_jiu_ge",
        "char_fairy_bai_qing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Sun and Moon Temple is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile equipment of Spirit Affinity House, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Heavenly Court reinforces against Myriad Year Flying Warship in the River of Time, Sun and Moon Temple arrives carrying Nine Spiritual Fairy beside Eternal Yacht. With that arrival Heavenly Court fields four rank eight Gu Immortals and six time path Immortal Gu Houses around the warship.",
      "chapters": [
        1882
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "river-of-time-reinforcement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "house_myriad_year_flying_warship",
        "loc_river_of_time",
        "char_nine_spiritual_fairy",
        "house_eternal_yacht",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "path_time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among Moment Stage, Present and Past Pavilion, Three Autumn Yellow Crane Platform, Eternal Yacht, Shark Flow Lever, and Sun and Moon Temple, Heavenly Court surrounds Myriad Year Flying Warship in the River of Time. After a grey stone giant destroys Present and Past Pavilion, it turns on Sun and Moon Temple. The house is weaker than the other time path Immortal Gu Houses present, fails to escape in time, and shatters in a second explosion, with most Gu Immortals inside killed.",
      "chapters": [
        1883
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "temple-destruction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_moment_stage",
        "house_present_and_past_pavilion",
        "house_three_autumn_yellow_crane_platform",
        "house_shark_flow_lever"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan dismantles Heavenly Court Immortal Gu Houses from that River of Time battle, the Immortal Gu in Sun and Moon Temple are Sun Day and Moon Month. Those gains sit with other recovered Immortal Gu that are mostly rank seven, with some rank eight.",
      "chapters": [
        1905
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "recovered-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_sun_day_immortal_gu",
        "gu_moon_month_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Above Emperor City during the Refinement Path Convention gathering, Ye Fan lists Sun and Moon Temple with Illusion Garden, Yue Yang Palace, and other floating Immortal Gu Houses as famous houses he can name.",
      "chapters": [
        1931
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
